# Layers

Writes go through services. Reads go through selectors. Simple properties and `Model.clean` may hold small checks. Ninja endpoints, schemas, `Model.save`, custom managers, and signals do not hold business logic.

```python
# ❌ BAD — the endpoint writes the row
@router.post("/users", response=UserOut)
def user_create(request, payload: UserIn) -> UserOut:
    user = User(email=payload.email, name=payload.name)
    user.save()
    return user

# ✅ GOOD — the endpoint calls the service
from apps.users import services

@router.post("/users", response=UserOut)
def user_create(request, payload: UserIn) -> UserOut:
    user = services.user_create(email=payload.email, name=payload.name)
    return user
```
